The untwisted family $X(u)$ has a proper flat Hausdorff analytic filling at $u=0$. Its corner winding is zero. The filling is obtained from two projective-line bundles by explicit plumbing, a proper modification and a finite quotient.
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.,leftmargin=*]
\item Let $S$ be the rational elliptic surface of Definition~\ref{I:def:pinching-data}, $M=\OO_S(P-O)$, $h=t_{6P}$, and $L=\Hom(h^*M,M)=\OO_S(F_\infty)$, with section $\phi$ vanishing on $F_\infty$. The absence of logarithmic twists gives $b=a=0$ in the corner character calculation. Thus the origins agree and their winding is zero. We now construct the filling with the untwisted finite fibres.

\begin{remark}[Topology determined by the fan data]\hypertarget{tag-02ZV}{}\label{push:src:A.4.5}\label{push:A45}
\StatementRecord{push:src:A.4.5}{proved}{02ZV}{\SeriesRef{push:src:A.2.4}, \SeriesRef{push:src:A.4.4}, \SeriesRef{push:src:A.4.7}, \SeriesRef{push:src:A.4.8}, \SeriesRef{push:src:A.4.9}}
For an output of Theorem~\ref{push:src:A.2.4},
Theorem~\ref{push:src:A.4.7} computes the Euler number, fundamental
group and nearby Euler function, and Theorem~\ref{push:src:A.4.8}
gives all integral homology groups and the marked monodromy.
Proposition~\ref{push:src:A.4.9} identifies the integral maps in the
normalization calculation through its direct-image splitting and
unit exceptional-fibre diagonals. All these calculations use the
same marked cone data.
\end{remark}

\hypertarget{tag-02ZF}{}\label{push:section:E.2}
\begin{remark}[The standard deformation theorem]
\hypertarget{tag-PI11}{}\label{I:standard-deformation-credit}
\StatementRecord{I:standard-deformation-credit}{proved}{PI11}{}
For the standard data $(\ell_0,\ell_1,\ell_2)=(0,1,-1)$,
the tangent dimensions and smooth reduced Kuranishi germ are given in
\cite[Theorem~6.12, pp.~81--82; Proposition~6.16, p.~85]{DuEtAl2026v1}.
The weighted calculation
also covers the coprime multiplicities stated below, and the
standard case includes the coarse tangent direct images.
\end{remark}

For the standard $(3,4)$ data, $e=\xi$ and the coarse direct
images are
\begin{equation}
 f_*T_X=\mathcal O\oplus\mathcal O(-1),\qquad
 R^1f_*T_X=\mathcal O\oplus\mathcal O(-1)^2,\qquad
 R^2f_*T_X=\mathcal O.
\label{pub:I:eq:D-4}
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}
